{
  "uid": "event-analytics-overview",
  "title": "Event Analytics \u2014 overview",
  "description": "The quantities a k6 run has to be reconstructable from without opening the journal, and whether the scrape that recorded them happened.",
  "tags": [
    "event-analytics"
  ],
  "annotations": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "Perf runs",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "grafana",
          "uid": "-- Grafana --"
        },
        "enable": true,
        "hide": false,
        "iconColor": "semi-dark-purple",
        "target": {
          "type": "tags",
          "matchAny": false,
          "tags": [
            "perf-run",
            "scrape:on"
          ],
          "limit": 1000
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "Perf runs measured with no scraper",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "grafana",
          "uid": "-- Grafana --"
        },
        "enable": false,
        "hide": false,
        "iconColor": "#8e8e8e",
        "target": {
          "type": "tags",
          "matchAny": false,
          "tags": [
            "perf-run",
            "scrape:off"
          ],
          "limit": 1000
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "editable": false,
  "refresh": "5s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-15m",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 100,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "The window shown",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Scrape",
      "description": "Whether the target answered every scrape in this window, not whether it answered the last one: min_over_time reads 1 only if no scrape in the window failed. The conservative reading is the useful one here, because a run measured across a dip is a run whose numbers are suspect, and \"was it ever up\" would hide the dip. Bounded by the window on purpose \u2014 a bare up is an instant selector, and Prometheus carries the last sample forward for five minutes, so it could not say \"not scraped\" until long after the scraper died.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 3,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "min(min_over_time(up{job=\"event-analytics\"}[$__range]))",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "1": {
                  "text": "up throughout",
                  "color": "green",
                  "index": 0
                },
                "0": {
                  "text": "dropped out",
                  "color": "red",
                  "index": 1
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "noValue": "not scraped"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Requests/s",
      "description": "Every /api/v1 route, ingest and read together, averaged over the whole window shown. Guarded with or vector(0) so an application that has served nothing yet reads 0 rather than No data: Micrometer registers a URI timer on the first request, while the ingest counters beside it exist from startup.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 3,
        "x": 3,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(rate(http_server_requests_seconds_count{uri=~\"/api/v1/.*\"}[$__range])) or vector(0)",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "mappings": [],
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Rejected/s",
      "description": "Requests a security filter turned away before handler mapping, averaged over the whole window shown. Spring tags them uri=\"UNKNOWN\", so they are in none of the /api/v1 panels, neither as traffic nor as errors, and a k6 run against an expired token otherwise reads as no traffic at all. Counted here rather than folded into the tiles beside it: widening their uri filter would let actuator traffic into the error-rate denominator and dilute it.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 3,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(rate(http_server_requests_seconds_count{status=~\"401|403\"}[$__range])) or vector(0)",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "mappings": [],
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Events/s",
      "description": "Both ingest paths, counted per event rather than per request, averaged over the whole window shown. Events accepted rather than rows written \u2014 a duplicate the unique constraint drops counts here too. The Ingest rate \u2014 events/s panel below carries the detail.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 3,
        "x": 9,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(rate(events_ingested_total[$__range])) or vector(0)",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "cps",
          "decimals": 0,
          "mappings": [],
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "p95 latency",
      "description": "Pooled across routes over the whole window shown, so it is not the same number as any single line on the latency panel below. A window that served nothing has no p95 in it at all and the tile reads No data \u2014 it no longer revives a value measured before the window and presents it as the current one.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(http_server_requests_seconds_bucket{uri=~\"/api/v1/.*\"}[$__range])))",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "decimals": 2,
          "mappings": [],
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Server error rate",
      "description": "Red above 0.01%, one server error in ten thousand requests, over the whole window shown. The numerator is guarded, so a service that has yet to serve a 5xx reads zero rather than No data. The denominator is not, so a window with no requests in it leaves the ratio undefined and the tile reads No data; the Scrape tile says whether that was an idle service or a stack that was not running.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "100 * (sum(rate(http_server_requests_seconds_count{uri=~\"/api/v1/.*\", outcome=\"SERVER_ERROR\"}[$__range])) or vector(0)) / sum(rate(http_server_requests_seconds_count{uri=~\"/api/v1/.*\"}[$__range]))",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "decimals": 2,
          "mappings": [],
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.01
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Peak pool pending",
      "description": "The deepest queue for a connection anywhere in the window, not the queue at its last sample. Red at one: the pool is the first thing to saturate under a spike, and a spike that queued in the middle of a run should not be erased by a calm end to it.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 20,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "max(max_over_time(hikaricp_connections_pending{job=\"event-analytics\"}[$__range]))",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "mappings": [],
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 101,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Throughput",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Ingest rate \u2014 events/s",
      "description": "Counted per event rather than per request, so the batch path reads at its real scale rather than at its request rate. Events accepted, though, not rows written: both paths insert with ON CONFLICT (event_id) DO NOTHING and neither reads the affected-row count, so a re-delivered event the unique constraint drops is counted here like any other and a replayed run reads as throughput. The paths also differ on when they count. The single path runs in no transaction, so its counter moves after the insert has already committed; the batch path counts the whole request inside its transaction, before the commit, so a batch that fails to commit is counted anyway.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (path) (rate(events_ingested_total[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{path}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "cps",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Ingest rate \u2014 requests/s",
      "description": "The same load per request. The gap to the panel beside it is the batch size in flight.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (uri) (rate(http_server_requests_seconds_count{uri=~\"/api/v1/events.*\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{uri}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Read rate \u2014 requests/s",
      "description": "The other half of the load. The ingest panels beside this one filter /api/v1/events.*, which is what makes the gap between them a batch size, so the read routes had nowhere to appear: three of the five read cells and the endpoint that saturates first ran with nothing on the dashboard moving. Split by uri, because the routes are not comparable \u2014 active-users is seconds where event-counts is milliseconds.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (uri) (rate(http_server_requests_seconds_count{uri=~\"/api/v1/stats/.*\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{uri}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 102,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Latency and errors",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 15
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Latency p95 / p99",
      "description": "Computed from bucket counts at query time, so the window is whatever this dashboard shows. Log scale, because the routes are three orders apart: over today's measurement pass p95 runs from 2.5 ms on /api/v1/events to 3.4 s on /api/v1/stats/active-users, and on a linear axis every write series lies flat on zero. Two quantiles across the five routes is ten legend rows, more than a table legend gets under a panel this tall, so it sits beside the plot instead \u2014 which also gives the log axis the full panel height.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 16
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, uri) (rate(http_server_requests_seconds_bucket{uri=~\"/api/v1/.*\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95 {{uri}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le, uri) (rate(http_server_requests_seconds_bucket{uri=~\"/api/v1/.*\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "p99 {{uri}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "scaleDistribution": {
              "type": "log",
              "log": 10
            }
          },
          "decimals": 2
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Error rate",
      "description": "Split by who failed: a rejected request is not a broken service. The numerator is guarded, so a service that has yet to serve a 5xx reads as zero rather than as No data. The denominator is not, so a window with no requests leaves the ratio undefined and the line breaks. A gap therefore means nothing was served, not that nothing failed \u2014 and the Scrape panel tells those cases apart: up at 1 beside the gap is an idle service, up at 0 is a service that was down, no up at all is a stack that was not running.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 16
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "100 * (sum(rate(http_server_requests_seconds_count{uri=~\"/api/v1/.*\", outcome=\"SERVER_ERROR\"}[$__rate_interval])) or vector(0)) / sum(rate(http_server_requests_seconds_count{uri=~\"/api/v1/.*\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "server",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "100 * (sum(rate(http_server_requests_seconds_count{uri=~\"/api/v1/.*\", outcome=\"CLIENT_ERROR\"}[$__rate_interval])) or vector(0)) / sum(rate(http_server_requests_seconds_count{uri=~\"/api/v1/.*\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "client",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "decimals": 2
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 103,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Saturation and scrape",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 25
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Connection pool",
